Subject: [PATCH 2/6] The production's wish and the season's audience are
 pinned where a seed search couldn't see them

Two reads had no test that a mutation of them would fail: the release answer's chance from how much the production
wants the actor back, and a grown part's chance from the season's audience. The journeys found their seeds through those
same functions, so a mutation moved the seed with the code and passed; each is now held by an assertion that reads the
function across its input (Exceptional against Working work, an audience over and under its bar, a played season's
audience off the bar). Forty-three mutations of the cluster's claims were run, one test file each; all were killed.

tests/journey-career.test.ts was left as it was, failing in this clone. Its seed v1-21 booked Desk Clerk from the August
2029 tape, judged Strong at 65.2 under a key holding the opportunity's id (`auditionContext`). With 9-1-1's guest part cast
only in seasons the game made, and v1-21's simulation canceling 9-1-1 in May 2029, the July 2 posting of it no longer
existed, every later id moved, and the same tape came out Working at 64.8; with the part posted as before, the booking
came back on 1 and 2 October. Re-finding the seed here would be undone by the other clusters' patches, which move the same
ids, and would collide with them in one file; it is the primary agent's to re-find once, after integration.

